<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dzungar genocide</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1755–1757</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> was the mass killing of the Dzungar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirat</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> by Qing forces in 1755–1757 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qianlong-emperor">Qianlong Emperor</a>. Together with epidemics and flight, it destroyed most of the Dzungar population and ended the Dzungar Khanate, allowing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> to incorporate the region into what became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dzungar-genocide.jpg" alt="Dzungar genocide" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A collaboration between Chinese and European painters. The Jesuit missionaries involved in producing the drawings in ... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dzungar_Tribe_Genocide.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
